From 46de287f91f48d66db46d182bfcb2962c3a03d7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Owen (via Claude Code)" <amasoonog@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:13:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ignore SQLite side files; untrack the committed WAL

.gitignore covers *.db, but jarvis.db-shm and jarvis.db-wal do not match that
pattern and were tracked. The WAL is 4 MB and holds rows from income,
investments, habit_log and marktplaats_messages, so the database the *.db rule
exists to keep out of the repo was being committed alongside it, and churned
on every run. Ignore the -shm/-wal/-journal side files and untrack both.

They remain in this repo's history.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018e7RTNjjvqCLb4X1QyVZTp
---
 .gitignore | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 3c5c0c7..432fa53 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -32,4 +32,12 @@ cookies.json
 *.db
 *.sqlite
 *.sqlite3
+# SQLite's side files do not match *.db, so they slipped through and were
+# committed - the -wal carries the same rows the *.db rule exists to keep out.
+*.db-shm
+*.db-wal
+*.db-journal
+*.sqlite-shm
+*.sqlite-wal
+*.sqlite-journal
 _backup-*/
-- 
2.43.0


--
NOTE: this patch carries only the .gitignore change. The commit it came from
also untracked two files, deliberately left out here because the -wal is a
4 MB binary holding rows from income, investments, habit_log and
marktplaats_messages -- embedding it in this patch would re-publish the data
the fix exists to remove. Apply the untracking by hand:

    git rm --cached server/jarvis.db-shm server/jarvis.db-wal
